# Line endings: LF on every platform for the files whose exact bytes ship in a package.
#
# src/CodeBrix.Platform.GameEngine.CardsAndDice.Assets embeds every file under Resources/, and
# catalog.json, as manifest resources, so whatever bytes are on disk at build time are baked into
# the assembly and shipped in the NuGet package. catalog.json pins each embedded file by its
# SHA-256 over LF bytes, and AssetCatalogTests checks every one. Without these rules a Windows
# clone under core.autocrlf=true expands the SVGs to CRLF on checkout, so a Windows build embeds
# different bytes from a Linux or macOS build and ships a catalog whose hashes do not match.
#
# The committed blobs are already LF. These rules only stop a checkout from expanding them.
*.svg   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# Never touched. Declared rather than left to git's heuristic, because a sound or image file
# that gets newline translation applied to it is silently corrupt.
*.ogg   binary
*.png   binary
